    How to tokenise
        -> On character or word or subword
        -> Byte Pair Encoding is the base algorithm on which all tokenisation algo are written
        -> In a document , it generates characters for each word marks end with _ or .
                -> Then it takes adjacent pairs and checks the no of occurence ..
                        highest occurences are merged to a token
                  Repeat above until vocab reaches its target size
        Does BPE guarantee linguistically meaningful splits? No,
         and this is a common misconception. BPE is a greedy, frequency-driven algorithm.


    An alternative called Unigram Language Model tokenization (used in SentencePiece, which powered earlier Llama and Google models) is probabilistic rather than greedy and tends to produce more linguistically coherent splits, b
    but neither approach is guaranteed to align with human intuitions about word structure.


